93,314,18,22,92,400,1939,37314,9960,510,27,37420,91339,397,1249,8253,1246,1657,4361,5109,2686,1091,17767,16,23,11,21,18,17,57758,525,30169,11680,311,17767,17,18,1124,79,2593,90,18,22,11035,701,582,1191,553,36710,1741,5109,304,279,1352,17767,77,284,220,18,22,74,488,220,17,18,57758,1380,17767,74,57758,374,264,2477,60935,7546,13,1205,1184,311,1477,279,7772,7546,17767,74,57758,1741,429,17767,77,366,220,16,23,11,21,18,17,59,3593,5338,11,582,738,705,279,31205,510,59,9640,18,22,74,488,220,17,18,366,220,16,23,11,21,18,17,198,59,921,3136,2144,220,17,18,504,2176,11067,510,59,9640,18,22,74,366,220,16,23,11,21,15,24,198,59,921,5847,11,21749,2176,11067,553,220,18,22,510,59,9640,74,366,1124,37018,90,16,23,11,21,15,24,15170,18,22,532,59,921,46951,279,12804,510,59,9640,59,37018,90,16,23,11,21,15,24,15170,18,22,92,1124,48053,220,20,15,18,198,59,921,12549,17767,74,57758,1969,387,458,7546,11,279,7772,3204,897,369,17767,74,57758,374,220,20,15,18,4192,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nHow many whole numbers less than $18,\\!632$ are congruent to $ 23 \\pmod {37} $?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine how many whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\), we start by expressing such numbers in the form \\(n = 37k + 23\\) where \\(k\\) is a non-negative integer. We need to find the largest integer \\(k\\) such that \\(n < 18,632\\).\n\nFirst, we set up the inequality:\n\\[\n37k + 23 < 18,632\n\\]\nSubtract 23 from both sides:\n\\[\n37k < 18,609\n\\]\nNext, divide both sides by 37:\n\\[\nk < \\frac{18,609}{37}\n\\]\nPerform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{18,609}{37} \\approx 503\n\\]\nSince \\(k\\) must be an integer, the largest possible value for \\(k\\) is 503.\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"00a9db067421f3b0229bec1006ecc61659e3d565fdc2e2b90ff41dcd246f45fc"},"seconds":21.86109209060669,"seed":1016794342132217838,"stop":"eos","text":"To find how many whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\), we start by representing these numbers in the form \\(n = 37k + 23\\), where \\(k\\) is a non-negative integer.\n\nFirst, we need to find the largest integer \\(k\\) such that \\(n < 18,632\\). This translates to the inequality:\n\\[\n37k + 23 < 18,632\n\\]\n\nSubtract 23 from both sides:\n\\[\n37k < 18,609\n\\]\n\nNext, divide both sides by 37:\n\\[\nk < \\frac{18,609}{37}\n\\]\n\nPerform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{18,609}{37} \\approx 503\n\\]\n\nSince \\(k\\) must be a non-negative integer, the largest possible value for \\(k\\) is 502 (as \\(k\\) must be strictly less than 503).\n\nNow, \\(k\\) can take any integer value from 0 up to 502, inclusive. To find the total number of such values, we count the integers in the range from 0 to 502:\n\\[\n502 - 0 + 1 = 503\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) that are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{503}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{503}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find how many whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\), we start by representing these numbers in the form \\(n = 37k + 23\\), where \\(k\\) is a non-negative integer.\n\nFirst, we need to find the largest integer \\(k\\) such that \\(n < 18,632\\). This translates to the inequality:\n\\[\n37k + 23 < 18,632\n\\]\n\nSubtract 23 from both sides:\n\\[\n37k < 18,609\n\\]\n\nNext, divide both sides by 37:\n\\[\nk < \\frac{18,609}{37}\n\\]\n\nPerform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{18,609}{37} \\approx 503\n\\]\n\nSince \\(k\\) must be a non-negative integer, the largest possible value for \\(k\\) is 502 (as \\(k\\) must be strictly less than 503).\n\nNow, \\(k\\) can take any integer value from 0 up to 502, inclusive. To find the total number of such values, we count the integers in the range from 0 to 502:\n\\[\n502 - 0 + 1 = 503\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of whole numbers less than \\(18,632\\) that are congruent to \\(23 \\pmod{37}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{503}\n\\]","id":"number_theory:92"}
